id: CTB-SRC0033-i1
source: SRC-0033
section: §2.1
kind: requirement
scope: ARC
title: Constitutional invariant I1: money integrity
applied-in: STG-00.A-1
text: Money integrity is constitutional invariant I1 and is never traded off: one exact money model with integer minor units and an explicit currency and scale, and every movement goes through a ledger, is reconciled and is never inferred. The money audit checks it (no float money in scope; ledgers balance), and CI and runtime guards enforce it.
